    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by the dual-threat upside of **Corbin Carroll** (69.89) and **Austin Riley** (69.46). **Corbin Carroll** remains an auto-start despite a negative platoon shift against Alec Gamboa, as his elite sprint speed and favorable park factors provide a floor that few others in our system can match. Conversely, **Austin Riley** sees a significant boost today against Ober, with the combination of a favorable 4.81 xERA matchup and wind blowing out at the stadium pushing his value deep into the \"Strong\" start tier. While his batting order slot is suboptimal, the situational data confirms he is our primary power threat for this slate.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was the retention of **Mickey Moniak** (45.58) in the UTIL slot. He barely avoided the bench, as his projection was severely hampered by a matchup against the elite Blake Snell (2.39 xERA) and a sharp negative platoon disadvantage. We opted to keep him active strictly for his park-adjusted potential and the hope that he avoids a Snell-induced slump, but he remains a high-variance play. We are monitoring **Gabriel Moreno** and **Henry Bolte** closely, as both rely on assumed batting orders; should **Henry Bolte** be pushed down from the leadoff spot, his 57.18 score would see a sharp downward revision, potentially rendering him a bench candidate.\n\nThe health status of our roster continues to be a concern, with **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Vinnie Pasquantino** all sidelined on the IL, leaving our depth thin as we push for Roto points. We are also tracking the availability of **Jose Caballero**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, and **Brice Turang** to see if they can provide late-inning speed or power bursts to mitigate the risks associated with the tough pitching matchups facing **Seiya Suzuki** and **Zach McKinstry**. With **Josh Naylor** off the board due to a team day off, we are leaning heavily on the speed-heavy profiles of our younger prospects like **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Cole Young**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Travis Bazzana** to bridge the gap in our categories as the season winds down.",
